          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/confidence-scoring.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Confidence Scoring\\ndescription: A qualitative reliability signal attached to a wiki page.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Confidence-Scoring\\n  - concept/Knowledge-Base\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Two sources; consistent on core rationale.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nConfidence scoring assigns a qualitative reliability signal to a page based on source count, source authority, and staleness.\\n\\n## Rationale\\n\\nThe score flags which pages deserve re-verification \\u2014 it is **not** a truth score. A confidence rating indicates which claims are well-sourced and which need corroboration, but does not pronounce a page \\u0027correct\\u0027 or \\u0027incorrect\\u0027. \\n\\nThe score is assigned at creation and revisited whenever new sources touch the same topic. Re-verification is the key action: confidence scoring directs attention where it is needed most.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Grimoire confidence-scoring system documentation.\\n\u0022}"
        }
